# Tests match the examples

A test calls the library the way the docs and samples do. The objects in the test are the ones a user writes: a connection, `ReadonlyRepository` or `CRUDRepository`, and `AddEnriched`.

Do not add a test repository that reimplements `Read`. Do not give the test a call that is absent from the examples.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — a test type that filters rows itself
var parents = new ListReadonlyRepository<Parent>(new Parent { id = 1 });
parents.AddEnriched(new("type_name", "type_id", "id", "name"), types);

// ✅ GOOD — the same construction as the sample
var parentsRepo = new ReadonlyRepository<Parent>(connection);
parentsRepo.AddEnriched(new("type_name", "type_id", "id", "name"), typesRepo);
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
const parents = new ListReadonlyRepository([parent(1, 10)]);

// ✅ GOOD
const parentsRepo = new ReadonlyRepository(Parent, connection);
parentsRepo.addEnriched({ into: "type_name", from: "type_id", by: "id", select: "name" }, typesRepo);
```
